explanation:
The definition builds the isomorphism one component at a time with `Hom.isoOfComponents`. Each component is `extend.XOpIso`. Naturality comes from `extend.XOpIso_hom_d_op`, which says the components commute with the differentials. This gives exactly the canonical comparison iso named in the docstring.

The setting is as general as the construction allows:
- any category with a zero object and zero morphisms (both are needed to define `extend`);
- any complex shapes c and c';
- any embedding between them.

Mathlib has no other declaration for this isomorphism. It is a standard compatibility isomorphism, not an error and not unnecessarily specialized.
